Rules added in pass 3 (all metadata-only; internal/specfix)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  null-type-in-array       Swagger 2.0 `type: [...]` containing "null" (3.1 spelling)
                           rewritten to the single real type + x-nullable, so the
                           2.0->3.0 conversion no longer copies an illegal 3.0 type
                           name. (weaviate)
  example-null-value       a null in an example where the owning schema declares a
                           concrete type and no nullability; a null on a REQUIRED
                           property drops the whole example (dropping the entry would
                           leave the required property absent). (docker)
  example-type-mismatch    generalised: the example is validated against its own
                           schema (references inlined) through kin-openapi; an
                           example the schema rejects is dropped. Covers out-of-enum,
                           out-of-format-range and string-vs-array element classes.
                           (docker, gitlab)
  example-missing-required array-level examples validated element-by-element against
                           the items schema (was object-level only). (gitlab)
  unknown-type             a `type` outside the Swagger 2.0 set ("text" from a
                           database/DTO leak) drops the type keyword and keeps every
                           other constraint; no type is invented. (gitlab)
  invalid-component-name   components/*/definitions names outside [a-zA-Z0-9._-]
                           (path-derived names) renamed and every $ref repointed.
                           (gitlab)
  wrong-bucket-ref         a response position referencing components/requestBodies
                           gets the referenced object copied into components/responses
                           under the same name (content byte-identical) and the
                           reference repointed. (pagerduty)
  default-type-mismatch    a schema-level or Swagger 2.0 parameter-level default the
                           schema rejects is dropped. (gitlab)
  non-schema scopes        security schemes (securityDefinitions /
                           components/securitySchemes), non-schema component buckets
                           and specification extensions (x-go-type) are never treated
                           as schemas — a regression guard found in this pass
                           (weaviate's security scheme lost its `type` before it).

algolia — why it stays rejected under tolerance
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The published entrypoint is not self-contained: its paths, schemas and
security schemes all live in sibling files (63 external $refs, e.g.
"paths/objects/common/schemas.yml#/attributeToUpdate"). The engine rejects any
external reference (openapi.DefaultParseOptions disallows them), and the
tolerance path must never fetch or invent target content:
  - fetching is out of scope (the opt-in repairs the document it was given),
  - dropping the referencing path/operation entries would delete API surface
    the author declared, which the metadata-only law forbids,
  - replacing them with empty path items would fabricate an API with zero
    endpoints.
So algolia is recorded as DOCUMENT-BLOCKED, not engine-blocked: the defect is
outside the document (it has no local content to repair), and specfix records
every external reference as an external-ref warning rather than rewriting it.
Loading it needs the multi-file bundle to be resolved by the caller first.

