Reading of the live proof: connect --tolerate loads docker with 20 tolerated
defects; `refresh` with no flags succeeds against the same document and reports
the same 20-defect summary (the opt-in is persisted on the connection, so no
flag is needed); `refresh --strict` fails, which proves the repair pass is what
makes the parse succeed rather than the document becoming parseable by itself.

